    {"id": "rail_climb", "occupied_offsets": [[0, 0, 0]], "support_offsets": [], "mount_sockets": [{"id": "rail_top", "type": "rail_mount", "offset": [0.0, 0.0, 0.0]}], "visual": {"color": "6f7880", "parts": [{"offset": [-0.22, 0.1, 0.0], "size": [0.1, 0.1, 1.0]}, {"offset": [0.22, 0.1, 0.0], "size": [0.1, 0.1, 1.0]}, {"offset": [0.0, -0.01, 0.0], "size": [0.6, 0.06, 0.1]}]}, "navigation": {"material_tags": ["wood", "breachable_wood"], "integrity": 30}, "dismantle_policy": "inventory_capacity_required", "defense": {"max_integrity": 30, "repair_item": "planks", "repair_amount": 6}, "coaster_tool": "climb", "attributes": {"value": 4, "role": "rail", "light": null, "mount": "any_solid_top", "space": [1, 1, 1], "notes": "CoasterCraft tracks: the Climb. Hold Right Mouse at the entry cell and the whole climb ghosts - a slope-in, a straight at any grade and a slope-out to a landing ahead and up (or down: a descent). Hold Shift and aim at the landing (a hilltop) to set its length and rise; 4-9 / X / C set the rise; W / R turn it. One Climb item per piece; the pieces are floating rail_loop curve pieces and plain rails join both ends."}},
